# C8 product-side relaxed scan: what does the perhydrate actually become?
#
# The plain relaxation (pc_bridge) ran away -- the transferring proton left O133
# entirely (O133-H132 -> 8.1 A, ending on the water at 0.75 A) and C128-O133
# collapsed to 1.313 A while C128=O129 stayed a carbonyl (1.212 A), with the
# energy still falling after 400 cycles (~0.9 Eh below the IRC endpoint). So
# "relax the IRC backward endpoint" does NOT land on a perhydrate minimum, and
# a longer relaxation would just keep running.
#
# This holds C128-O133 and lets everything else relax, mapping the product basin
# without the runaway. Range 1.25-2.10 A brackets the collapsed species (1.31),
# the IRC backward endpoint / putative perhydrate (1.42), and the separated
# limit (1.92 at the forward endpoint).
#
# Full system (no ActiveAtoms), 21-atom QM1, same as the bridge TS.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) Opt TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{55 58 61 64 120 121 122 123 124 125 126 127 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
  Scan
    B 128 133 = 1.25, 2.10, 11
  end
  MaxIter 200
  Calc_Hess true
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
